    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0421" n="1235" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg1235"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">PPS files, lot 64
                    D 563, “Atomic Energy–Armaments”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Policy Planning
                        Staff (Bowie) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d117-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-10-30">October 30, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>Subject:</item>
                    <item>Conversation with Admiral Strauss</item>
                </list>
                <p>Admiral Strauss wishes to discuss
                    with you the possibilities of a new approach to the international control of
                    atomic energy. The attached memorandum briefly reviews: <pb facs="0422" n="1236"
                        xml:id="pg1236"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>a.</label>
                        <item>The problem;</item>
                        <label>b.</label>
                        <item>The plan endorsed by the U.S. for dealing with it;</item>
                        <label>c.</label>
                        <item>The Russian position; and</item>
                        <label>d.</label>
                        <item>A suggestion for a new approach which Admiral Strauss has privately put
                            forward.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert
                                R. Bowie</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d117-a1.xml" xpointer="d117-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d117-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d117-f1-content">
                <p>The source text is accompanied by a typed, unsigned, and undated note, which
                    reads: “Mr. Bowie says this just hits
                    the ‘high spots’ but might be helpful before you see Admiral Strauss this morning. Admiral Strauss’ proposal is at Page 6.”
                    According to the Secretary’s appointment book, he met with Bowie and Strauss at 10:10 a.m., Oct. 31. (Princeton University Library,
                        Dulles papers, “Daily
                    Appointments”)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
